1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,882
Aarav turns the dial on his
grandfather's old radio.

2
00:00:03,882 --> 00:00:06,482
The air is full of stations at once.

3
00:00:06,832 --> 00:00:10,810
Yet with one small turn, he hears
just one of them, loud and clear.

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:14,259
How does the radio pick
one station out of so many?

5
00:00:14,859 --> 00:00:19,641
The secret is a circuit with a resistor,
a coil and a capacitor in series.

6
00:00:19,991 --> 00:00:22,029
Each one opposes the current.

7
00:00:22,029 --> 00:00:25,055
The total opposition
is called impedance, Z.

8
00:00:25,405 --> 00:00:27,237
It is measured in ohms.

9
00:00:27,237 --> 00:00:30,535
But you cannot simply add R, XL and XC.

10
00:00:30,535 --> 00:00:31,699
Let's see why.

11
00:00:32,349 --> 00:00:36,601
Here is the circuit on the breadboard,
on a ten volt supply whose frequency

12
00:00:36,601 --> 00:00:37,525
we can turn.

13
00:00:37,875 --> 00:00:40,158
At fifty hertz, XC is large.

14
00:00:40,158 --> 00:00:41,998
Very little current flows.

15
00:00:42,348 --> 00:00:43,898
Turn the frequency up.

16
00:00:43,898 --> 00:00:47,214
XL grows, XC shrinks,
and the current climbs.

17
00:00:47,564 --> 00:00:52,379
At about one hundred and fifty
nine hertz, XL and XC become equal.

18
00:00:52,379 --> 00:00:53,383
They cancel.

19
00:00:53,733 --> 00:00:54,989
Only R is left.

20
00:00:54,989 --> 00:00:58,475
The current jumps to its
biggest value, one ampere.

21
00:00:59,125 --> 00:01:01,422
Keep going, and XL takes over.

22
00:01:01,422 --> 00:01:03,095
The current falls again.

23
00:01:03,445 --> 00:01:06,882
The graph of current against
frequency has a sharp peak.

24
00:01:06,882 --> 00:01:08,813
This peak is called resonance.

25
00:01:09,463 --> 00:01:11,426
Watch the scope at the peak.

26
00:01:11,426 --> 00:01:14,180
Voltage and current
rise and fall together.

27
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:15,538
They are in phase.

28
00:01:16,188 --> 00:01:19,427
At resonance, the coil
and the capacitor cancel.

29
00:01:19,427 --> 00:01:20,671
Only R is left.

30
00:01:21,471 --> 00:01:24,549
Now the formula for
impedance, in small steps.

31
00:01:24,899 --> 00:01:28,068
In the resistor, voltage
and current are in step.

32
00:01:28,068 --> 00:01:31,674
In the coil, voltage leads
the current by ninety degrees.

33
00:01:32,374 --> 00:01:35,890
In the capacitor, voltage
lags by ninety degrees.

34
00:01:35,890 --> 00:01:40,232
So the coil and capacitor voltages
point in opposite directions.

35
00:01:40,932 --> 00:01:42,059
They subtract.

36
00:01:42,059 --> 00:01:45,671
The net push from them
is I times XL minus XC.

37
00:01:46,371 --> 00:01:48,604
This is at right angles to IR.

38
00:01:48,604 --> 00:01:50,768
So we join them with Pythagoras.

39
00:01:51,468 --> 00:01:56,558
Z equals the square root of R
squared, plus XL minus XC, squared.

40
00:01:57,258 --> 00:02:03,101
The phase angle, phi, follows from
tan phi equals XL minus XC, over R.

41
00:02:03,801 --> 00:02:06,795
For resonance, set XL equal to XC.

42
00:02:06,795 --> 00:02:09,922
Two pi f L equals one over two pi f C.

43
00:02:10,622 --> 00:02:15,464
So the resonant frequency is f naught
equals one over two pi, root LC.

44
00:02:15,464 --> 00:02:18,581
There, Z equals R, the smallest it can be.

45
00:02:19,231 --> 00:02:20,480
Worked example.

46
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:26,432
R is thirty ohms, XL is eighty ohms,
and XC is forty ohms, on a one hundred

47
00:02:26,432 --> 00:02:27,513
volt supply.

48
00:02:27,863 --> 00:02:29,852
XL minus XC is forty.

49
00:02:29,852 --> 00:02:33,567
Z is the root of thirty
squared plus forty squared.

50
00:02:33,567 --> 00:02:35,141
That is fifty ohms.

51
00:02:35,741 --> 00:02:38,983
The current is one
hundred divided by fifty.

52
00:02:38,983 --> 00:02:40,057
Two amperes.

53
00:02:40,657 --> 00:02:45,429
And tan phi is forty over thirty,
so phi is about fifty three degrees.

54
00:02:45,429 --> 00:02:48,839
XL is bigger, so the
voltage leads the current.

55
00:02:49,489 --> 00:02:50,858
Back to the radio.

56
00:02:50,858 --> 00:02:53,852
Its tuning circuit is
a coil and a capacitor.

57
00:02:54,202 --> 00:02:56,833
Turning the dial changes the capacitance.

58
00:02:56,833 --> 00:03:00,800
Only the station at the resonant
frequency gets a big current.

59
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:02,580
All the others stay tiny.

60
00:03:03,230 --> 00:03:04,696
Now, the exam trap.

61
00:03:05,046 --> 00:03:09,200
Many students say that at resonance,
the impedance becomes zero and the

62
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:10,779
current becomes infinite.

63
00:03:11,129 --> 00:03:12,029
No.

64
00:03:11,654 --> 00:03:13,754
Only the reactances cancel.

65
00:03:13,754 --> 00:03:18,639
Z becomes R, its smallest value,
and the current is V over R.

66
00:03:19,289 --> 00:03:20,809
Where is this asked?

67
00:03:20,809 --> 00:03:23,543
In PUC board papers, and in JEE Main.

68
00:03:23,543 --> 00:03:28,042
Find Z, the current, the phase
angle, or the resonant frequency.

69
00:03:28,692 --> 00:03:29,592
Try this.

70
00:03:29,570 --> 00:03:34,952
A series circuit has L equals forty
millihenry, C equals twenty five microfarad,

71
00:03:34,952 --> 00:03:38,975
and R equals twenty ohms, on
a one hundred volt supply.

72
00:03:38,975 --> 00:03:42,763
At resonance, what are the
frequency and the current?

73
00:03:48,163 --> 00:03:49,063
C.

74
00:03:48,579 --> 00:03:52,074
One hundred and fifty nine
hertz, and five amperes.

75
00:03:52,424 --> 00:03:54,969
L times C is ten to the minus six.

76
00:03:54,969 --> 00:03:57,924
Its square root is ten to the minus three.

77
00:03:58,274 --> 00:04:01,764
So omega naught is one
thousand radians per second.

78
00:04:01,764 --> 00:04:06,885
Divide by two pi, and f naught is
about one hundred and fifty nine hertz.

79
00:04:07,235 --> 00:04:09,148
At resonance, Z equals R.

80
00:04:09,148 --> 00:04:13,287
The current is one hundred over
twenty, which is five amperes.

81
00:04:13,937 --> 00:04:15,459
Screenshot this card.

82
00:04:18,659 --> 00:04:20,146
Next, transformers.

83
00:04:20,146 --> 00:04:24,849
How does the grey box on an electric
pole change thousands of volts into

84
00:04:24,849 --> 00:04:26,735
the supply for our homes?
